course: dictionary
lesson: 11818
title: Two metals in one
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller words. Bi means two, and metallic means made of metal, so bimetallic means made of two metals. «The strip is bimetallic: two different metals are stuck together.» Look for the small words inside a long word, and they often give you the meaning.
explain: Scientists use bimetallic strips because of heat. «When the strip got hot, it bent.» One metal grows a little more than the other when heated, so the joined strip curves. That bending is the clue that tells you the strip has two metals.
explain: The word also has a second meaning, about money and history. «Long ago, some countries used both gold and silver as money.» In that sense, bimetallic describes a money system, not a strip or a coin. Always check which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Bimetallic means made of two different metals joined together.
fact: Bi means two, and metallic means made of metal.
fact: A bimetallic strip bends when it is heated, because one metal grows more than the other.
fact: Thermostats, fire alarms and some kettles use bimetallic strips to switch things on or off.
fact: In money and history, bimetallic means using both gold and silver as the basis of money.
exercise: «The bimetallic strip bent when the kettle got hot.» What does bimetallic mean? | Made of plastic and glass | Cold and shiny | Made of one metal only | *Made of two different metals joined together
exercise: Why does a bimetallic strip bend when it is heated? | *Because one metal grows more than the other | Because someone pushes it | Because it is painted | Because the metal melts into water
exercise: «Long ago, some countries were bimetallic, using gold and silver as money.» What does bimetallic mean here? | Made of wood and paper | Only using coins from one country | *Using both gold and silver as the basis of money | Shiny and new
test: «The £2 coin is bimetallic, with two colours.» What does bimetallic describe? | Two different sizes of paper | A pencil with two ends | A book with two covers | *A coin made of two different metals joined together
test: Which of these uses a bimetallic strip to switch on or off? | A bicycle chain | A bookshelf | *A thermostat | A pencil case
exam: «The strip is bimetallic.» Which description is correct? | Made of wood and glass | Made of one metal only | Painted in two colours only | *Two different metals stuck together
